+## Access observations and exact preservation scope
+
+The **2,808,814-byte EADXML** has SHA256 **64fe584a77626718747b0bd0e799798fbfe30ebe0b13f8d95ba1dc8efa8bff91**. Its item **aspace_VAB8595-01172** links this memo under Briefing Books → June17 military hearing materials. Title-level searches did not identify the March2004NORADletter; that is not an exhaustive contents search or evidence of absence.
+
+The first linked-item request returned **HTTP401**. A later request declaring a research User-Agent returned **HTTP200** and a **12,846-byte manifest**, SHA256 **8aaa1954f928bcef123276ec2153cf6161202d2dac7aca137aee51aafd48795e**. Both outcomes are preserved. Request conditions and time differed; this observation does not establish the cause of the first response. No credentials, login, cookies, proxies or private endpoints were used.
+
+The manifest's PDF-export link returned **HTTP200 / text/html**, an **805-byte human-verification page**, not a PDF. That body remains preserved; the challenge was not interacted with or retried. A generic renderer's initial one-page interpretation of that HTML was not accepted as a PDF page count. Source inspection instead used the separately published IIIF image service. Each image was requested at1600pixels wide through its declared ImageAPI2 size parameter; these are **page-image derivatives, not master scan bytes**. [IIIF size contract](https://iiif.io/api/image/2.1/#size).
+
+All twelve responses were JPEGs and are preserved unchanged in the guarded media store, totaling **4,972,992bytes**. Whole-page images **1,9,10,11,12** were visually read. All twelve pages received localOCR for navigation; the other seven were locator-screened only. OCR is a derivative and does not replace the images. Exact image URLs, canvas IDs, dimensions, access times, hashes and OCR locators are in [SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json). Raw images, fullOCR, archive XML, access-error bodies, connection information and PDF-export response are excluded from publication.
